+/* Pillar-change loading screen (PillarLoading.jsx): the brand diamond breathing on
+   the dark ground while a pillar chunk resolves.
+   INSTANT AND SOLID ON FRAME ONE - no entrance delay, no fade-in. The first cut
+   waited 140ms then faded, on the theory that a warm chunk would resolve unseen and
+   an instant loader would strobe. Frame forensics killed that theory: a cold pillar
+   sat with an EMPTY body at 135ms and only filled by ~690ms, so the delay bought
+   nothing and simply moved the blank frame around - the wait is always real enough
+   to show (owner report + scratchpad filmstrip, build 257).
+   The breath therefore starts AT full strength and dips, rather than starting dim,
+   so nothing about the first frame reads as a fade. It animates opacity + transform
+   ONLY: unlike the boot splash's one-off drop-shadow glow, this runs on every
+   pillar change, and a paint-phase animation there would raster the region every
+   frame (§6). */
+/* VIEWPORT-CENTRED, deliberately, because a pillar wait has TWO phases and they do
+   not share a box: first the chunk loads (the mark sits in the empty pillar column,
+   measured 813px tall), then the pillar mounts its own header and reports its own
+   loading state (measured 519px, since min-height governs once the parent is no
+   longer a stretching flex column). Centring in each box moved the mark 105px UP
+   between the two - the "snaps upwards" the owner saw. Anchoring to the viewport
+   instead makes the position identical in both phases and on every screen.
+   Safe here: the pillar slide animates OPACITY only, so no ancestor creates a
+   containing block (verified on device - transform/filter/perspective all none).
+   pointer-events:none because a transient full-viewport layer must never eat a tap,
+   and no z-index, so nav (40), dock (50) and sheets (200) still paint above it. */
+.cx-pillar-load { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding-bottom: 8vh; pointer-events: none; }
+.cx-pillar-load-mark { animation: cxMarkBreath 1.9s ease-in-out infinite; will-change: opacity, transform; }
+@keyframes cxMarkBreath { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); } 50% { opacity: .62; transform: scale(.955); } }
+/* Still fallback - the mark stays fully legible, it just stops breathing. */
+body.reduce-motion .cx-pillar-load-mark, body.reduce-motion .cx-pillar-load { animation: none; opacity: 1; transform: none; }
+@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .cx-pillar-load-mark, .cx-pillar-load { animation: none; opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
